# Restaurant Digital Platform — Development Rules

Follow `DEVELOPMENT_RULES.md` in the project root. Non-negotiable highlights:

## Security & tenancy
- Never bypass RLS. Never trust client `restaurant_id` or prices.
- Derive restaurant access from authenticated `restaurant_members` membership via guards — not hard-coded demo IDs.
- Calculate order totals server-side. Never store raw card data. Verify payments server-side.
- Validate all external input (Zod at API boundaries).

## Data & types
- TypeScript strict; avoid `any`.
- Do not hardcode restaurant data, currency, or timezone.
- Store timestamps in UTC; display in restaurant timezone.

## AI (Phase 1)
- Use approved DB tools only; never invent metrics.
- AI cannot directly modify production data.
- Owner must approve AI-generated content before publishing.

## Scope & quality
- No Phase 2/3 features unless explicitly requested.
- Test business logic and tenant isolation; never disable tests to pass build.
- No secrets in code; never commit `.env` files.

## Process
- Prefer simple architecture. Document important decisions.
- Review `ARCHITECTURE.md` before architectural changes (create/update it when making structural changes).
- Schema changes require a new migration in `supabase/migrations/`.
- No destructive DB changes without explicit user approval.

## Known Phase 1 violations to fix, not extend
- Dashboard/API uses `getDemoRestaurantId()` instead of membership — violates rules 2, 3, 12.
- `guardRestaurantRoute()` exists but is unwired in API routes — violates rules 3, 4.
